```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Background Image Display</title>
    <style>
        body {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            height: 100vh;
            width: 100vw;
            overflow-x: hidden;
            overflow-y: hidden;
            font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
            background-color: #f4f4f4; /* Background color for the whole window */
            transition: transform 2s ease-in-out; /* Smooth transformation animation */
        }
        .container {
            position: relative;
            height: 100%;
            width: 100%;
        }
        img {
            position: absolute;
            top: 50%;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
            max-width: 100%;
            max-height: 100%;
            object-fit: cover; /* Ensures the image fills the container while maintaining aspect ratio */
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<button id="displayImage">Display Background Image</button>

<div class="container">
    <img src="" alt="Your Background Image Here" id="backgroundImage" />
</div>

<script>
document.getElementById('displayImage').addEventListener('click', function() {
    const backgroundImage = document.querySelector('#backgroundImage');

    // Get the URL of the background image from the system
    var url = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement).getPropertyValue('--image-url');

    if (url) {
        backgroundImage.src = url;
        backgroundImage.style.transform = 'translateX(0%) translateY(0%)';
    } else {
        alert("No background image found.");
    }
});
</script>

</body>
</html>
```

### Explanation:
- **HTML Structure**: The structure includes a `button` with the ID `displayImage` and a `div` containing the `img` element where the background image will be displayed.

- **CSS Styling**:
  - `body`: Sets up the viewport dimensions and styles to prevent horizontal scrolling.
  - `.container`: Defines the layout of the main content area.
  - `img`: Positions the image absolutely in the center of the parent div (`body`) and ensures it scales properly without distortion.

- **JavaScript**:
  - Adds an event listener to the button that triggers when clicked.
  - Uses `window.getComputedStyle` to get the value of `--image-url`, which is typically defined somewhere in your CSS file or through a JavaScript variable.
  - If the URL is valid, it sets the source of the image and animates its positioning smoothly using CSS transitions.

To use this code:
1. Save it as an HTML file (e.g., `index.html`).
2. Open the saved file in a web browser.
3. Click the "Display Background Image" button to see the image appear as your background.

Make sure to define the `--image-url` property either in your CSS or dynamically via JavaScript so it points to a valid image URL.

